<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia posts 1H rise in international air cargo.</title>
<headline>Colombia posts 1H rise in international air cargo.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>International air cargo in and out of Colombia increased 11.82 percent in the first half of this year compared to the same period of 1996, the Civil Aviation Authority said Thursday.</p>
<p>In the January to June period 102,844 tons were flown into Colombia -- a 16.37 percent gain. Outbound air cargo was up 8.13 percent to 117,609 tons.</p>
<p>Domestic air cargo volume, however, fell 6.71 percent in the same period to 63,527 tons.</p>
<p>((-- Karl Penhaul, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
